    "text": "To determine the combined length of the CDs that James buys, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the length of the first two CDs.\n2. Determine the length of the third CD.\n3. Add the lengths of all three CDs together.\n\nStep 1: Identify the length of the first two CDs.\nEach of the first two CDs is 1.5 hours long. Therefore, the total length of the first two CDs is:\n\\[ 1.5 \\text{ hours} + 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the length of the third CD.\nThe third CD is twice as long as one of the first two CDs. Since each of the first two CDs is 1.5 hours long, the third CD is:\n\\[ 2 \\times 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nStep 3: Add the lengths of all three CDs together.\nThe combined length of the three CDs is the sum of the lengths of the first two CDs and the third CD:\n\\[ 3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} = 9 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nTherefore, the combined length of the CDs is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
